===High-speed lines===
{{Main|High-speed rail in Qym}}

As of {{abbr|2440|2027 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, [[High-speed rail in Qym|Qym's high-speed rail network]]<!--Aqant Gelis Ryba, Express Rail Line--> comprises 4 lines in service, 2 under construction, and 3 planned lines. The [[AGR South|first line]] was inaugurated in {{abbr|2387|1983 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, connecting the capital, [[Zhol]], with the [[OCEAN NAME]] city of [[Nagur]] to the south. The [[AGR West|second line]] was inaugurated in {{abbr|2400|1994 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, connecting the capital, [[Zhol]], with the city of [[Patsalys]] to its west. The [[AGR East|third line]] was inaugurated in {{abbr|2409|2001 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, connecting the capital, [[Zhol]], with the city of [[Byvichek]] to its east. The [[AGR Southeast/west|fourth line]] was inaugurated in {{abbr|2423|2013 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, connecting the capital, [[Zhol]], with the city of [[Teurek]] to its southeast/west. Two lines have been under construction since {{abbr|2420|2010.36 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, connecting [[Zhol]] with [[Leramy]] and with [[Tulim]], and scheduled to open in {{abbr|2445|2031 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. In a break from the previously [[Zhol]]-centric network, a planned 7th line would connect [[Nagur]] with [[Teurek]], while an 8th would connect [[Balc]] and [[Krosnica]], and a 9th the cities of [[Kalnuj]] and [[Narylce]].

